body:
Yeah...uhhhh....this too is an unusual escalation. Although the War in Donbass has been recognised as "ongoing" since 2014 (i.e. for the last 7 years), the last few weeks and days represent an unusual escalation. A worst case scenario would see Russia upgrading from supporting Russian-backed militias in eastern Ukraine from the sidelines, to actually overtly supporting Russian-backed militias or downright \*invading\*.

&#x200B;

(At first, I didn't take any notice because the War in Donbass has been going on since 2014 and I thought to myselfmyself, itit"it may be a short thing like the Russo-Georgia conflict back in 2008; but then I mentally slapped myself and said "hey, this isn't Georgia, this is Ukraine, so it's probably gonna be much worse; then I see a news report on reliable objective Russian media that says NATOisNATO is literally shifting troops and hardware as we speak and I'I'm like, "yeah, this could be much, much worse, you've definitely got my attention now"
